{"seq":13,"trial_id":"v03-installer-dev-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-30T15:23:50.742Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"024f3b82eeaed6447308fef1edf0d26dfeccbfdb675285d14462d15b22da25d3","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03INS0001","text":"Dana, I found two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines in Moss's notes:\n\n- **#PD-4492**: Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" note (dated 5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell submitted it on 4 Oct for gatehouse kiosk SMS bay assignments at the Eau Claire yard, Dock Doors 14 to 18. Support patched it, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the 04:00 shift cleared. The note also lists a product triage action to review it before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n- **#4419**: Moss's undated \"North cheat sheet.\" Thea logged it for gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nOutside Moss's notes, a note by Marcus Lindqvist (Q2 expansion wrap, 14 Jul 2025) also mentions #4419, but describes it as Gate 3 printer lag. That conflicts with the cheat sheet's description, so you may want to check which is right before it goes in the weekly notes. I left that note out of the list because it isn't Moss's.\n\nThe brain search is keyword-only, so a note that describes a ticket without these terms could have been missed."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03INS0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
